From 95979897506aea93bab064851fe68cbe1e13f918 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:27:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] ui: FPS picker sends only set_fps during a speed-ramp
 take

Why: with Core's fps_ramp on (T31), the FPS picker is a ramp control in
cDNG and MLV takes. applyFps() followed every set_fps with its own
set_shutter_us to keep the angle and saved the result. In a ramp take that
undoes Core's Exposure shutter policy (setShutterUs also clears the
nominal exposure Core keeps across the ramp) and saves a take-scoped rate
as the operator's setting, which Core avoids since T31 (Cinemate ff59dd8).
What: the bridge reads fps_ramp from Core's state and settings replies.
In a take with fps_ramp on, applyFps() sends set_fps and stops; Core sets
the shutter by its policy, the reply (already applied by sendCoreCommand)
updates FPS and shutter on screen, and Core restores and persists the
take's start rate at stop. Outside ramp takes nothing changes.
ensureValidFpsSelection() returns early with a bridge, so in-between rates
from a stepper (26, 27 ...) are not "corrected" by the UI.

Tested: host build of the whole UI with Qt 6.4.2 (QML compiled ahead of
time). Not run on the Pi.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T93jucKMhWYnQM1yyFVkbH
---
 src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 src/ApertarControlBridge.hpp |  1 +
 2 files changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp b/src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp
index 3a4a59a..e6b95b2 100644
--- a/src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp
+++ b/src/ApertarControlBridge.cpp
@@ -270,6 +270,13 @@ bool ApertarControlBridge::applyFps(const QString &displayValue)
     if (!sendCoreCommand(QStringLiteral("set_fps"), { { QStringLiteral("value"), fpsValue } }, &fpsReply))
         return false;
 
+    // A ramp step in a take (T31): Core applies the shutter policy (angle or
+    // exposure) and restores the take's start rate at stop, and sendCoreCommand has
+    // already applied its reply. Send nothing more: a set_shutter_us here would undo
+    // the exposure policy, and saving would make a take-scoped rate the setting.
+    if (m_recording && m_fpsRamp)
+        return true;
+
     setFps(formatFpsValue(fpsValue));
     if (m_shutterAuto) {
         setShutterAngle(QStringLiteral("Auto"));
@@ -1358,6 +1365,9 @@ void ApertarControlBridge::applyCoreState(const QJsonObject &state)
     if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("shutter_auto")))
         m_shutterAuto = state.value(QStringLiteral("shutter_auto")).toBool(m_shutterAuto);
 
+    if (state.contains(QStringLiteral("fps_ramp")))
+        m_fpsRamp = state.value(QStringLiteral("fps_ramp")).toBool(m_fpsRamp);
+
     const double ev = state.value(QStringLiteral("exposure_compensation")).toDouble(m_exposureCompensation);
     const bool evAvailable = state.value(QStringLiteral("exposure_compensation_available")).toBool(m_exposureCompensationAvailable);
     if (ev != m_exposureCompensation || evAvailable != m_exposureCompensationAvailable || previousAutoExposure != autoExposureEnabled()) {
diff --git a/src/ApertarControlBridge.hpp b/src/ApertarControlBridge.hpp
index 9a5bcf0..f483a9d 100644
--- a/src/ApertarControlBridge.hpp
+++ b/src/ApertarControlBridge.hpp
@@ -315,6 +315,7 @@ private:
     QString m_exposureMetering = QStringLiteral("centre-weighted");
     QVariantList m_exposureMeteringOptions;
     bool m_recording = false;
+    bool m_fpsRamp = false; // Core's fps_ramp (T31): FPS may change during a raw take
     bool m_recordingHasDroppedFrames = false;
     bool m_standby = false;
     QString m_coreMediaState;
